            "items": [
              {
                "title": "About the Wallabies",
                "text": "Australia played its first Test in 1899, against a touring British Isles side at the Sydney Cricket Ground. The name Wallabies comes from the 1908 tour of Britain and has stayed with the men’s team ever since.\n\nThe Wallabies won the Rugby World Cup in 1991 and again in 1999, the first team to lift the trophy twice. They have played New Zealand for the Bledisloe Cup since 1932, and meet New Zealand, South Africa and Argentina every year in The Rugby Championship.",
                "link": {
                  "label": "Our history",
                  "href": "/history"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        },
